# Whether anything wants the AWDL radio. Written by barqsharingd, read by barqd.
#
# A property rather than binder: barqd holds CAP_NET_ADMIN and CAP_NET_RAW, and a
# property read is a shared-memory load of one boolean -- no parser, no IPC surface
# in the privileged process. See barqd's WANT_PROP comment for why this is also not
# ctl.start/ctl.stop.
# Prefix, not one exact key: the namespace now carries the Wi-Fi frequency as well
# as the wanted flag, and an exact rule for one leaves the other on default_prop --
# where set_prop on our own type is still denied, which fails silently.
barq.awdl.          u:object_r:barq_awdl_prop:s0

# The advertised device name. Prefix for the same reason as above: an exact rule for
# one key leaves any sibling on default_prop, where set_prop on our own type is still
# denied and fails silently -- which is exactly how this one was found, with the
# settings screen appearing to accept a name that never reached the property.
persist.barq.       u:object_r:barq_name_prop:s0
